WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:05.760
Can a psychological thriller work as a musical?&nbsp;
Can a high budget action flick be successfully&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:11.158
broken into two parts? We'll be sure to&nbsp;
find out once these 2024 films hit screens.

00:00:11.158 --> 00:00:15.540
If anything should put directors Anthony&nbsp;
and Joe Russo's upcoming sci-fi epic "The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:20.400
Electric State" on viewers' watchlists, it's&nbsp;
the extraordinary cast. Millie Bobby Brown&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:24.420
and Chris Pratt are slated to play the lead&nbsp;
roles, but it's in the supporting cast where&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:28.860
things get really enticing. The film will&nbsp;
feature an ensemble cast of actors in both&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:34.140
live-action and voice-over roles, including&nbsp;
Ke Huy Quan, Brian Cox, and Jenny Slate.

00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:37.440
On top of all that, former "Seinfeld" star Jason&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:41.820
Alexander will also be making a rare major&nbsp;
motion picture appearance in the feature.

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:46.415
"Take me to your leader." Laughs.

00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:50.880
Outside of the cast, it will also be interesting&nbsp;
to see how the Russos translate the striking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:55.560
imagery of Simon Stålenhag's "Electric State"&nbsp;
graphic novel into a film adaptation. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.560 --> 00:01:00.420
images from the source material make use of&nbsp;
evocative deep blue hues and feature massive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:05.280
robots lingering around in everyday environments,&nbsp;
leaving a lot of opportunities for the filmmakers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:10.380
to produce equally striking cinematography through&nbsp;
which they can tell this unique sci-fi story.

00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:15.480
Adrian Molina's days at Pixar date back to&nbsp;
2007 when he worked as an animator on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:19.140
end titles of "Ratatouille." Since then,&nbsp;
Molina has moved up in the ranks at Pixar&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:23.640
to provide additional screenplay material for&nbsp;
"The Good Dinosaur" and "Monsters University."

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:28.020
He also served as co-director and&nbsp;
screenwriter on the 2017 smash hit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:33.060
"Coco." Come 2024, Molina will move up&nbsp;
to solo directing Pixar's upcoming title,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.060 --> 00:01:37.260
"Elio." Details on the project are minimal, but&nbsp;
according to Pixar's official Twitter account,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.260 --> 00:01:41.580
the film will be a sci-fi yarn about&nbsp;
a young boy who winds up in the far&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:46.620
reaches of outer space and gets mistaken by&nbsp;
alien lifeforms as the ambassador for Earth.

00:01:46.620 --> 00:01:50.580
"Coco" was such an extraordinary and&nbsp;
well-renowned feature that the prospect&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.580 --> 00:01:55.380
of any new production from Molina should be enough&nbsp;
of a reason for Pixar fans to celebrate. It will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.380 --> 00:01:58.980
also be interesting to see Pixar's next&nbsp;
take on the world of sci-fi storytelling,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.980 --> 00:02:03.000
a domain the studio has explored sporadically&nbsp;
throughout the years to varying results.

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:08.760
For example, "Wall-E" was a fairly resounding&nbsp;
success when it came out in 2008. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.760 --> 00:02:12.840
their more recent attempt at a sci-fi&nbsp;
story, 2022's "Lightyear," received&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.840 --> 00:02:17.340
mixed reviews at best. With so many promising&nbsp;
elements even this early into its production,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:22.980
"Elio" has the potential to be another storied&nbsp;
chapter in Molina's prolific career at Pixar.

00:02:22.980 --> 00:02:28.080
It's been a while since audiences got&nbsp;
to explore the vast and imaginative&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:32.700
world of Miles Morales depicted in 2018's&nbsp;
"Spider-Man: Into the Spider-Verse." However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:37.320
not only is a sequel to that movie imminent,&nbsp;
but a pair of follow-ups are also on the docket.

00:02:37.320 --> 00:02:42.480
The second sequel set in the "Spider-Verse"&nbsp;
universe will be "Spider-Man: Beyond the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:47.640
Spider-Verse," which is scheduled to hit theaters&nbsp;
in March 2024. Given how scant few details are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:52.080
available about the first of these sequels,&nbsp;
"Spider-Man: Across the Spider-Verse," it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:56.880
no surprise that "Beyond the Spider-Verse" is&nbsp;
shrouded in mystery. Most information about which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.880 --> 00:03:01.320
characters from the first two films will appear in&nbsp;
the third is still not public knowledge, though it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:06.660
has been confirmed that Jason Schwartzman's Spot&nbsp;
will serve as the main villain in the 2024 film.

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:12.360
Still, the vibrancy of this world makes the&nbsp;
concept of spending more time in the multiverse&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.360 --> 00:03:18.360
of Spider-people incredibly exciting. Plus,&nbsp;
the title "Beyond the Spider-Verse" suggests&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.360 --> 00:03:25.140
some truly trippy storytelling possibilities&nbsp;
could be in store for audiences. We'll have to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:28.920
wait and see to find out more about what&nbsp;
this particular movie has up its sleeve,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.920 --> 00:03:32.100
but if the quality of "Into the&nbsp;
Spider-Verse" is any indication,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:36.420
audiences should get stoked for what&nbsp;
"Beyond the Spider-Verse" has in store.

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:41.040
"Look, I made a promise. So, I have to keep it."

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:46.800
The world of "A Quiet Place" is poised to expand&nbsp;
significantly with the forthcoming spin-off,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.800 --> 00:03:52.140
"A Quiet Place: Day One." While details about&nbsp;
this film's plot are still largely under wraps,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.140 --> 00:03:56.220
it does appear that new characters beyond the&nbsp;
original "Quiet Place" protagonists will be taking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.220 --> 00:04:01.560
center stage, with Lupita Nyong'o and Joseph Quinn&nbsp;
lined up to play two of the new film's leads.

00:04:01.560 --> 00:04:03.960
There's also change afoot behind the scenes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.960 --> 00:04:08.460
with "Pig" writer and director Michael&nbsp;
Sarnoski taking over John Krasinski's place&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.460 --> 00:04:14.220
as director. With such vast shifts in casting&nbsp;
and leadership, this next installment to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:18.300
"Quiet Place" universe could offer something&nbsp;
noticeably different from its predecessors.

00:04:18.300 --> 00:04:22.500
The title suggests that moviegoers will&nbsp;
be returning to the very start of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.500 --> 00:04:27.180
noise-sensitive alien invasion, a backdrop&nbsp;
briefly explored in the prologue to "A Quiet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.180 --> 00:04:31.740
Place: Part II." Exploring how humans react to&nbsp;
their suddenly changing world could certainly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.740 --> 00:04:35.640
provide a fresh spin for the franchise,&nbsp;
especially since Sarnoski proved to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.640 --> 00:04:39.780
extremely gifted at exploring humanity's&nbsp;
ability to grapple with loss in "Pig."

00:04:39.780 --> 00:04:45.960
Ethan Hunt, the protagonist of the expansive&nbsp;
"Mission: Impossible" series, has had to pull&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.960 --> 00:04:51.300
off some incredible feats throughout this&nbsp;
franchise. However, soon Tom Cruise's iconic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:56.160
character will have to complete an especially&nbsp;
daunting task: nailing a two-part blockbuster.

00:04:56.160 --> 00:04:59.520
The next installment in the "Mission:&nbsp;
Impossible" franchise, "Dead Reckoning,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:04.140
is going to be split across a pair of motion&nbsp;
pictures, the second of which will arrive in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.140 --> 00:05:08.340
June 2024. As titles like "Divergent:&nbsp;
Allegiant" have proved in the past,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.340 --> 00:05:13.920
taking one story and splitting it across two&nbsp;
movies can go very wrong very fast. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.920 --> 00:05:18.720
if Hunt could climb the world's tallest building&nbsp;
and survive, then it stands to reason he might&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.720 --> 00:05:22.140
manage to make "Dead Reckoning" a&nbsp;
satisfying multi-film experience.

00:05:22.140 --> 00:05:26.400
"How am I supposed to do this?" Glove smacks.

00:05:26.400 --> 00:05:30.120
One promising aspect of the second part&nbsp;
of "Dead Reckoning" is that it will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.120 --> 00:05:33.540
feature some cast members that won't&nbsp;
be around for the first installment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.540 --> 00:05:36.600
including Nick Offerman and Holt McCallany.

00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:40.860
The presence of new faces indicates that&nbsp;
the second part of "Dead Reckoning" might&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.860 --> 00:05:45.960
just offer something unique, rather than&nbsp;
act as a rehash of the first part. That's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.960 --> 00:05:50.520
just one of the countless reasons moviegoers&nbsp;
are on the edge of their seats waiting for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.520 --> 00:05:53.580
"Mission Impossible – Dead Reckoning&nbsp;
– Part Two" to show up in theaters.

00:05:54.180 --> 00:06:00.300
After dominating the Academy Awards, Bong Joon&nbsp;
Ho returns to both science-fiction cinema and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.300 --> 00:06:05.760
English-language storytelling with his 2024&nbsp;
directorial effort, "Mickey 17." Based on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.760 --> 00:06:10.980
book "Mickey7" by Edward Ashton, "Mickey&nbsp;
17" stars the endlessly versatile Robert&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:10.980 --> 00:06:16.560
Pattinson as a man tasked with working on an&nbsp;
expedition to colonize a far-off ice planet.

00:06:16.560 --> 00:06:22.080
From there, if prior Joon Ho movies are any&nbsp;
indication, the film is likely to take some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.080 --> 00:06:25.920
unpredictable turns and project potent&nbsp;
social commentary on the world around&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.920 --> 00:06:31.260
us. There are still so few details on what this&nbsp;
adaptation will look and feel like, but Joon Ho's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.260 --> 00:06:36.060
incredible body of work makes it difficult not&nbsp;
to get tantalized by this project immediately.

00:06:36.060 --> 00:06:38.760
If the film's elevator pitch&nbsp;
wasn't enough to excite you,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.760 --> 00:06:43.200
the rest of the cast just might. Aside from&nbsp;
Robert Pattinson taking on the lead role,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:43.200 --> 00:06:48.420
Toni Collette, Steven Yeun, Naomi Ackie, and&nbsp;
Mark Ruffalo are all listed as supporting cast.

00:06:48.420 --> 00:06:54.120
Pattinson has always shown a penchant for working&nbsp;
with beloved auteurs like David Cronenberg, Robert&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.120 --> 00:06:59.100
Eggers and Claire Denis, so it's incredibly&nbsp;
exciting to imagine what he'll accomplish as a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.100 --> 00:07:03.540
performer working under the filmmaker responsible&nbsp;
for "Parasite." Needless to say, there are more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.540 --> 00:07:08.460
than a few reasons to be pumped for the release of&nbsp;
this legendary director's next cinematic effort.

00:07:08.460 --> 00:07:13.800
"Furiosa" is a new George Miller movie.&nbsp;
That fact alone should send it rocketing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:13.800 --> 00:07:18.180
toward the very top of any list of the&nbsp;
most anticipated movies of 2024. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.180 --> 00:07:22.200
fact that it's a George Miller directorial&nbsp;
effort set in the "Mad Max" world, however,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.200 --> 00:07:26.100
makes the prospect of this cinematic&nbsp;
experience even more appetizing.

00:07:26.100 --> 00:07:30.900
This time around, the character of Furiosa from&nbsp;
"Mad Max: Fury Road" will not be portrayed by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:30.900 --> 00:07:35.760
Charlize Theron, but by Anya Taylor-Joy. This&nbsp;
leading lady has been on a hot streak with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:35.760 --> 00:07:41.460
her work in movies and TV, including notable 2022&nbsp;
titles like "The Northman" and "The Menu." So, the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:41.460 --> 00:07:45.780
idea of her getting to work under the direction&nbsp;
of George Miller sounds downright extraordinary.

00:07:45.780 --> 00:07:50.460
"Care for a demonstration?"
 
English actor Thom Burke will also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:50.460 --> 00:07:55.560
appear in the film's cast. While Burke may not be&nbsp;
a household name yet, he delivered extraordinary&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.560 --> 00:08:00.240
work in Joanna Hogg's "The Souvenir." With a&nbsp;
background largely in British indies and TV,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.240 --> 00:08:05.220
it will be extremely revelatory to see what he&nbsp;
can do with a much larger canvas at his disposal

00:08:05.220 --> 00:08:10.560
Beyond the cast, which also includes Chris&nbsp;
Hemsworth, "Furiosa" is bound to be home to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.560 --> 00:08:15.840
a practically realized spectacle that only Miller&nbsp;
would have the gall and imagination to pull off.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.840 --> 00:08:21.300
If he manages to capture even a fraction of the&nbsp;
"Fury Road" magic, then "Furiosa" will be only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:21.300 --> 00:08:26.880
the latest example of why any new George Miller&nbsp;
movie should be met with great anticipation.

00:08:26.880 --> 00:08:31.020
The "Planet of the Apes" franchise has&nbsp;
seen seemingly constant updates over the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:31.020 --> 00:08:34.680
course of the last few decades, which might&nbsp;
make viewers think that this saga would be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.680 --> 00:08:39.300
running on fumes creatively. However, the most&nbsp;
recent trilogy of features from this universe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:39.300 --> 00:08:42.120
two of which were helmed by "The&nbsp;
Batman" director Matt Reeves,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:42.120 --> 00:08:45.240
were some of the most exciting&nbsp;
and daring entries to date.

00:08:45.240 --> 00:08:49.560
That's not to say "Planet of the Apes" is&nbsp;
incapable of churning out a dud movie — Tim&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:49.560 --> 00:08:54.120
Burton's 2001 film "Planet of the Apes" was&nbsp;
certainly a lacking contribution to the franchie.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:54.120 --> 00:08:58.500
However, there's clearly a lot of creative&nbsp;
longevity within this universe, which makes the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:58.500 --> 00:09:04.020
prospect of the 2024 installment "Kingdom of the&nbsp;
Planet of the Apes" sound especially appetizing.

00:09:04.020 --> 00:09:08.220
According to Deadline, "Kingdom of the Planet&nbsp;
of the Apes" will take place decades after the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:08.220 --> 00:09:13.140
events of "War for the Planet of the Apes," though&nbsp;
any further plot details are wrapped up in secrecy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:13.140 --> 00:09:18.120
for now. However, the idea of a continuation&nbsp;
of the story first established in "Rise of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:18.120 --> 00:09:22.200
the Planet of the Apes" is certainly compelling.&nbsp;
Additionally, with Wes Ball as the new director,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.200 --> 00:09:26.940
there's plenty of possibility for some fresh new&nbsp;
visuals to be incorporated into this installment.

00:09:26.940 --> 00:09:31.320
What's more, Owen Teague is tapped to play the&nbsp;
main ape, and his remarkable work in features&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:31.320 --> 00:09:36.180
like "To Leslie" makes us enthusiastic to see what&nbsp;
he'll do in a motion-capture role. To summarize,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:36.180 --> 00:09:40.740
there are plenty of reasons to go bananas&nbsp;
for "Kingdom of the Planet of the Apes."

00:09:40.740 --> 00:09:46.380
After finally taking on the mantle of Captain&nbsp;
America in the final episode of "The Falcon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:46.380 --> 00:09:51.660
and the Winter Soldier," Sam Wilson will get to&nbsp;
headline his own feature film in "Captain America:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:51.660 --> 00:09:56.880
New World Order." Directed by "Luce" filmmaker&nbsp;
Julius Onah, "Captain America: New World Order"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:56.880 --> 00:10:01.560
promises to continue some of the most intriguing&nbsp;
elements of "The Falcon and the Winter Soldier."

00:10:01.560 --> 00:10:04.980
However, "New World Order" is also&nbsp;
primed to connect Wilson's Captain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:04.980 --> 00:10:09.120
America to broader parts of the Marvel&nbsp;
Cinematic Universe mythology, like the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:09.120 --> 00:10:13.320
long-awaited return of Tim Blake Nelson's&nbsp;
Samuel Stern from "The Incredible Hulk."

00:10:13.320 --> 00:10:18.900
This Marvel Studios feature is also positioned&nbsp;
to include the debut appearance of Harrison Ford&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:18.900 --> 00:10:25.740
as General Thaddeus "Thunderbolt" Ross. Just the&nbsp;
presence of such a legendary acting giant should&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:25.740 --> 00:10:30.660
put "New World Order" on many a viewer's radar.&nbsp;
However, the fact that it will also function as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:30.660 --> 00:10:35.280
an opportunity to see the new Captain America&nbsp;
soar as a big-screen leading man is without a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.280 --> 00:10:39.420
doubt the primary cause of the buzz that&nbsp;
has already begun surrounding this film.

00:10:39.420 --> 00:10:47.460
The Dragon Warrior is back. In March 2024, Po&nbsp;
will return for another adventure in "Kung Fu&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:47.460 --> 00:10:51.720
Panda 4." That's all that anybody in the general&nbsp;
public knows about this forthcoming sequel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:51.720 --> 00:10:56.340
with even key details like the creative team&nbsp;
behind this follow-up shrouded in mystery.

00:10:56.340 --> 00:11:00.240
However, ambiguity certainly won't keep&nbsp;
people from getting excited about all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:00.240 --> 00:11:04.740
the possibilities of seeing Po go on another&nbsp;
epic quest. After all, the first three "Kung&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:04.740 --> 00:11:08.760
Fu Panda" movies are among the strongest&nbsp;
titles in the DreamWorks Animation canon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:08.760 --> 00:11:13.380
with "Kung Fu Panda 2" standing out as a sequel&nbsp;
that took the franchise in a new tonal direction&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:13.380 --> 00:11:17.880
without losing the core ingredients that&nbsp;
made the original installation so loveable.

00:11:18.404 --> 00:11:22.424
"You gotta let go of that stuff from&nbsp;
the past, cause it just doesn't matter."

00:11:22.740 --> 00:11:27.660
If the "Kung Fu Panda" franchise could pull&nbsp;
off a sequel as good as "Kung Fu Panda 2,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:27.660 --> 00:11:31.620
then there's a good chance "Kung Fu Panda&nbsp;
4" could also be something special. Plus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:31.620 --> 00:11:35.280
recent DreamWorks Animation titles&nbsp;
like "The Bad Guys" and "Puss in Boots:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:35.280 --> 00:11:40.440
The Last Wish" have been remarkably strong&nbsp;
in overall quality. If that hot streak of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:40.440 --> 00:11:44.220
creativity extends to this forthcoming&nbsp;
"Kung Fu Panda" feature, then audiences&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:44.220 --> 00:11:48.840
should prepare themselves for another totally&nbsp;
awesome addition to the "Kung Fu Panda" saga.

00:11:48.840 --> 00:11:53.100
The Marvel Cinematic Universe has&nbsp;
often concerned itself with totally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:53.100 --> 00:11:56.400
unknown superheroes who've never been&nbsp;
considered for the big screen before,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:56.400 --> 00:12:00.660
like the Guardians of the Galaxy or the&nbsp;
Eternals. However, one of its upcoming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:00.660 --> 00:12:05.580
2024 titles will be anchored by a superhero who&nbsp;
has not only appeared in a feature film before,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:05.580 --> 00:12:10.800
but actually led a trilogy of movies&nbsp;
across the late 1990s and early 2000s.

00:12:10.800 --> 00:12:16.500
A new incarnation of Blade, once played&nbsp;
by Wesley Snipes, is headed to the MCU,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:16.500 --> 00:12:20.460
with this version of the character being&nbsp;
played by Mahershala Ali. According to The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:20.460 --> 00:12:24.240
Hollywood Reporter, the two-time Oscar&nbsp;
winner has such a deep passion for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:24.240 --> 00:12:28.320
character that he outright asked Marvel&nbsp;
Studios to let him play the vampire hunter.

00:12:28.320 --> 00:12:31.860
While Ali's commitment to "Blade"&nbsp;
has never wavered in the years&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:31.860 --> 00:12:36.840
since he signed onto the role, the movie&nbsp;
itself has experienced several hardships&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:36.840 --> 00:12:41.160
on its way to the screen, including the&nbsp;
loss of original director Bassam Tariq.

00:12:41.160 --> 00:12:45.840
While those setbacks have been discouraging,&nbsp;
the choice of Yann Demange as the new director&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:45.840 --> 00:12:49.800
of the film inspires a lot of confidence&nbsp;
that this feature could still turn out to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:49.800 --> 00:12:54.000
be something special. Additionally, Marvel&nbsp;
Studios has successfully delivered several&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:54.000 --> 00:12:58.440
classics in spite of turbulent productions&nbsp;
in the past, so there are still a few good&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:58.440 --> 00:13:02.280
reasons to remain hopeful that Ali's stint&nbsp;
as Blade will turn out to be a success.

00:13:02.280 --> 00:13:08.100
"The Fall Guy" originated as a TV show starring&nbsp;
Lee Majors that aired on ABC for five seasons&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:08.100 --> 00:13:13.920
in the 1980s. In March 2024, though, it'll be&nbsp;
released as an action movie headlined by Ryan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:13.920 --> 00:13:18.480
Gosling and helmed by "Bullet Train" director&nbsp;
David Leitch. However, Gosling isn't the only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:18.480 --> 00:13:23.580
recognizable name in this action feature:&nbsp;
Emily Blunt, Stephanie Hsu, Winston Duke,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:23.580 --> 00:13:28.380
Aaron Taylor-Johnson, and Hannah Waddingham&nbsp;
are all set to round out the ensemble cast.

00:13:28.380 --> 00:13:33.660
"The Fall Guy" is so far out from release that&nbsp;
many aspects of the production are still unknown,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:33.660 --> 00:13:37.200
including just how much or how&nbsp;
little this motion picture will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:37.200 --> 00:13:41.100
adhere to its source material. However,&nbsp;
any opportunity to watch Ryan Gosling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:41.100 --> 00:13:46.080
punch people sounds like a good time at the&nbsp;
movies, and the supporting cast sounds ace.

00:13:46.080 --> 00:13:50.820
Leitch's filmmaking career has had its ups&nbsp;
and downs, but the best of his works have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:50.820 --> 00:13:55.740
had a propulsive energy and zippy atmosphere&nbsp;
that's difficult to resist. Plus, his peak&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:55.740 --> 00:14:01.260
effort as an auteur, 2017's "Atomic Blonde,"&nbsp;
also featured incredible fight choreography,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:01.260 --> 00:14:06.900
which could indicate "The Fall Guy" will feature&nbsp;
cool combat sequences at the very least. All in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:06.900 --> 00:14:12.480
all, the ingredients are there for this movie to&nbsp;
be much more than a rehash of a 1980s TV staple.

00:14:12.480 --> 00:14:16.140
The original "Joker" may not&nbsp;
have been everybody's cup of tea,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:16.140 --> 00:14:20.460
but it undeniably separated itself from&nbsp;
the typical comic book movie adaptation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:20.460 --> 00:14:25.020
genre and remained a topic of cultural&nbsp;
discussion for years after its release.

00:14:25.020 --> 00:14:30.420
After years of speculation over whether or not a&nbsp;
sequel to "Joker" would ever hit movie theaters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:30.420 --> 00:14:36.060
its follow-up is officially scheduled to come&nbsp;
out in October 2024. Another key figure from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:36.060 --> 00:14:40.320
the the villain's comic book lore, Harley&nbsp;
Quinn, will also play a role in the film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:40.320 --> 00:14:45.480
with Lady Gaga portraying her. On top&nbsp;
of that, this follow-up, entitled Joker:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:45.480 --> 00:14:49.740
Folie à Deux [foh-LEE AH DOO] will also be a&nbsp;
musical, which will allow the movie to indulge&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:49.740 --> 00:14:54.240
Gaga's talents as a singer and differentiate&nbsp;
itself immensely from its predecessor.

00:14:54.240 --> 00:14:59.460
While the concept of making a "Joker" sequel&nbsp;
may sound predictable, it's safe to assume&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:59.460 --> 00:15:03.720
few fans of the original were expecting&nbsp;
a musical to follow it. Additionally,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:03.720 --> 00:15:08.040
the idea of Lady Gaga playing a version of&nbsp;
Harley Quinn with even a fraction of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:08.040 --> 00:15:12.120
energy and passion the performer brought to&nbsp;
her "House of Gucci" performance sounds even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:12.120 --> 00:15:17.820
more exciting. "Joker: Folie à Deux" is bound&nbsp;
to be as divisive as its predecessor, but it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:17.820 --> 00:15:22.860
also sounds like the kind of sequel that swings&nbsp;
for the fences rather than sits on its laurels.

00:15:22.860 --> 00:15:29.640
"Ha ha ha ha ha ha ha ha ha&nbsp;
ha ha ha ha ha ha ha ha!"

00:15:29.640 --> 00:15:35.160
After "Titanic," audiences had to wait 12&nbsp;
years for a new James Cameron movie. After&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:35.160 --> 00:15:40.440
"Avatar," moviegoers had to wait another 13&nbsp;
years to experience a fresh vision from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:40.440 --> 00:15:45.840
filmmaker. A significantly shorter wait will exist&nbsp;
between "Avatar: The Way of Water" and Cameron's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:45.840 --> 00:15:51.120
next directorial effort, the untitled third&nbsp;
"Avatar" movie set for a December 2024 release.

00:15:51.120 --> 00:15:55.080
While Cameron is keeping many details&nbsp;
of "Avatar 3" close to the vest,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:55.080 --> 00:15:58.680
Collider reports that this film will&nbsp;
introduce some new characters poised&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:58.680 --> 00:16:02.880
to make waves throughout the entire swath of&nbsp;
"Avatar" sequels. David Thewlis is slated to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:02.880 --> 00:16:07.080
play a Na'vi character that will debut in this&nbsp;
film, while characters played by Michelle Yeoh&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:07.080 --> 00:16:10.200
and Oona Chaplin will also premiere&nbsp;
in this installment of the franchise.

00:16:10.200 --> 00:16:15.180
Cameron's penchant for extravagant spectacle&nbsp;
in the first two "Avatar" movies should make&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:15.180 --> 00:16:19.320
it clear that this upcoming sequel will&nbsp;
continue working to that effect. It's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:19.320 --> 00:16:23.160
also exciting to know that "Avatar 3" will&nbsp;
introduce new characters instead of just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:23.160 --> 00:16:28.800
leaning on familiar figures from the franchise's&nbsp;
past. There's still so much to see on Pandora,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:28.800 --> 00:16:33.480
and that makes the idea of returning to the&nbsp;
planet in "Avatar 3" an immensely rousing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:33.480 --> 00:16:38.400
concept, especially since it will arrive much&nbsp;
sooner than the previous films in the series.

00:16:39.600 --> 00:16:40.980
"Outstanding."

